---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteImage from '../components/SiteImage.astro';
---
<Layout title="About Neev Grover" description="Neev Grover is the student inventor behind DuneBroom, a low-cost AI vision rover that measures shoreline trash density.">
<main id="main-content">
      <section class="py-16 max-w-[860px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight text-foreground mb-12 mt-0">
          About
        </h1>

        <div class="flex gap-8 items-start mb-10 flex-wrap">
          <SiteImage
            src="/neev_profile.png"
            alt="Neev Grover, founder of DuneBroom"
            width={160}
            height={160}
            class="rounded-full bg-surface shrink-0"
          />
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-[240px]">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight mb-1 mt-0">Neev Grover</h2>
            <p class="text-base text-subtle mb-4 mt-0">Founder · Junior at the Harker School</p>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
              I&apos;m a student inventor who likes using technology to solve real environmental
              problems. I built DuneBroom from the ground up: I designed the rover and camera
              system, trained its debris-detection model, wrote its counting algorithms, and led
              school outreach programs across India. Outside of engineering, I play competitive
              chess, write about technology, and build projects that make a tangible impact.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-border mb-10" />

        <div class="mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight mb-4 mt-0">The mission</h2>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted mb-4">
            I started DuneBroom to build a robot that picks trash off beaches. Building it showed
            me a more basic problem: without accurate, consistent measurement, communities
            can&apos;t tell whether cleanup efforts are reducing trash at all. So I redesigned
            DuneBroom as a low-cost rover that measures shoreline trash density, letting
            researchers and local agencies survey more often and compare results over time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Along the way, the project grew into something larger: an education and awareness program reaching
            450+ students across 5 schools in India, a children&apos;s book, and a drawing
            competition that gave young people a creative voice in the fight for a cleaner planet.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-border mb-10" />

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          {[
            { value: "450+", label: "Students reached" },
            { value: "5", label: "Partner schools" },
            { value: "1", label: "Book published" },
            { value: "2+", label: "Years of research" },
          ].map(({ value, label }) => (
            <div class="bg-surface p-5 rounded-xl border border-border">
              <span class="figure block text-[28px] font-medium text-foreground leading-none mb-2">
                {value}
              </span>
              <span class="text-[13px] text-muted">{label}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
